{"event_type":"review","id":"b1f678f6700de503eb4261bac33582dbe08803b4cf00b43dae7529c1c1d4f4cc","occurred_at":"2026-11-17T01:38:32Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7a24a43b7ac9bf0cc742e194dfe1211d12cde88fe70266f9bd1fa75d9a871601","sha256":"7a24a43b7ac9bf0cc742e194dfe1211d12cde88fe70266f9bd1fa75d9a871601"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/504bc6d7c4e5f0a5ed1bd3e4c5247d05fe674b0eff9040e7501c8a89d3b18532","sha256":"504bc6d7c4e5f0a5ed1bd3e4c5247d05fe674b0eff9040e7501c8a89d3b18532"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b55c5a10472f22aef8bd0f6bea12d68e40fb939b91db1b907c43a6a268806aa6","sha256":"b55c5a10472f22aef8bd0f6bea12d68e40fb939b91db1b907c43a6a268806aa6"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b952fa0f279eb978702705b09f5040ded57fc6c7dfaee2e0ba4ae1eadcec8273","sha256":"b952fa0f279eb978702705b09f5040ded57fc6c7dfaee2e0ba4ae1eadcec8273"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/61e512c5cd30b600926361191f8a7e863397469676460dc3864e5c4bb2e33a21","sha256":"61e512c5cd30b600926361191f8a7e863397469676460dc3864e5c4bb2e33a21"}],"attempt_id":"f0133de07ec52307a412b996cd8dfe0e4f5ac53b7827144694e0ee104dc32ece:0:1","base":"af9ccb974e2ea08760fdbaaeb7c7355ff0bba8da","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"576f3ff4afb69cd85e103c3d46c1a4229ee54088","body":"**Add the owner check to the `cancel` route before calling `cancelRequest`.**\n\n`cancelRequest` looks up the request by `request_id` alone. Nothing in the `cancel` route compares the request's `principal` with the caller. Any principal in `policy.write` can therefore withdraw another principal's notification and cancel that principal's pending item when no observers remain. `notify-update` rejects this same case, so the two routes enforce different rules. Add the same binding check to `cancel`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     case 'cancel': {\n-      const cancelled = cancelRequest(queue, stringRequired(request, 'request_id'), withdrawNotify);\n+      const requestId = stringRequired(request, 'request_id');\n+      const binding = readRequest(queue, requestId);\n+      if (binding === null || binding.get('principal') !== principal) {\n+        throw new ValueError('cancel request owner denied');\n+      }\n+      const cancelled = cancelRequest(queue, requestId, withdrawNotify);\n```\n\n</details>","id":"bfc911b5ff5cf36c20f835999d317dfb701fa2624c54e12a7092ccfbb9a24cbe","intervals":[[274,274]],"path":"src/ops/crq/reviewCapability.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Add the owner check to the `cancel` route before calling `cancelRequest`."}],"head":"040eeee5df7a8c8113ecade6c0baf5400f3cf239","head_tree":"2a6378f38614c8b16a7d30447cf71e2ddc2985f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"576f3ff4afb69cd85e103c3d46c1a4229ee54088","intervals":[[1,980]],"path":"src/ops/crq/reviewCapability.ts"}],"job_id":"f0133de07ec52307a412b996cd8dfe0e4f5ac53b7827144694e0ee104dc32ece:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"576f3ff4afb69cd85e103c3d46c1a4229ee54088","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/crq/reviewCapability.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"576f3ff4afb69cd85e103c3d46c1a4229ee54088","intervals":[[560,585],[596,596],[901,902]],"path":"src/ops/crq/reviewCapability.ts"}],"reviewed_scope":[{"blob":"576f3ff4afb69cd85e103c3d46c1a4229ee54088","intervals":[[560,585],[596,596],[901,902]],"path":"src/ops/crq/reviewCapability.ts"}],"scope_digest":"0c25e80ae6548ebc8550c2a4fdecf6989b683b65b6ea00ca14706457172d5672","source":{"authenti